{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For their vine is from the vine of Sodom, and from the fields.</b> He doubled the expression, for 'fields' are vines, as it is written (Isaiah 16): ״כי שדמות חשבון אומלל גפן שבמה״, and likewise (Habakkuk 3): ״ושדמות לא עשה אוכל״. And he said this concerning the nations, for their root is evil and bitter, and how can the grapes be sweet? For since the vine is the vine of Sodom, the grapes will surely be grapes of rosh (gall), and the wine too the venom of serpents."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:24.607873861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}